Article 6 (Planning and Coordination Division)
(1) The head of the Planning and Coordination Division shall be appointed at Grade 3 or Grade 4.
(2) The head of the Planning and Coordination Division shall take charge of the following matters:
1. Establishment, integration, and coordination of major work plans of the Commission;
2. Inspection and management of various instructions and government tasks within the Commission;
3. General coordination of affairs related to the National Assembly;
4. Formulation and request of the budget, coordination of execution, and settlement of accounts;
5. Appointment, service, education and training, and other personnel affairs of public officials;
6. Management of the organization and personnel ceilings within the Commission;
7. Matters concerning the composition and operation of the Commission;
8. Disclosure of information, management of records, and operation of archives;
9. General coordination of informatization affairs within the Commission;
10. Management of state-owned property and goods, budget operation, and accounting;
11. Contracts and expenditures for goods, services, construction works, etc.;
12. Establishment and implementation of public relations plans and monitoring of media reports;
13. Support for external policy announcements and briefings concerning Commission affairs;
14. Management and operation of statutes and regulations related to the Commission and general coordination of litigation affairs;
15. Matters concerning coordinated management of ordinances of local governments in metropolitan areas;
16. General coordination of cooperation with local governments in metropolitan areas;
17. Other matters not under the jurisdiction of any other department of the Metropolitan Area Transport Headquarters.
